From 5bcfac95f668f7eadc169f4b7a133d3d4034e78d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Buddhabhatti <jay.buddhabhatti@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 18 Aug 2025 04:59:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 035/190] drivers: firmware: xilinx: Switch to new family code
 in zynqmp_pm_get_family_info()

commit 3c48fb669dd1f81d9a4c9e8a11aed2dd4b310497 from
https://github.com/Xilinx/linux-xlnx.git xlnx_rebase_v6.12

Currently, the family code and subfamily code are derived from the
PMC_TAP_IDCODE register. As a result, Versal, Versal NET, and Versal
Gen2 share the same family code, and Versal NET and Versal Gen 2 share
the same subfamily code, making it difficult to distinguish between
platforms. Update zynqmp_pm_get_family_info() to use IDs derived from
the compatible string instead of silicon ID codes derived from
PMC_TAP_IDCODE register.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20250701123851.1314531-4-jay.buddhabhatti@amd.com
Signed-off-by: Jay Buddhabhatti <jay.buddhabhatti@amd.com>
State: upstream (88fa7c8181bd5c5738eb22b0e144d5b1fef2ee20)
Message-ID: <20250818115901.3692021-6-jay.buddhabhatti@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Quanyang Wang <quanyang.wang@windriver.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
